182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (This report details a deep learning approach for automatic speech emotion detection \(SED\), a key element in affective computing and human-computer interaction. The project develops a robust neural network for identifying seven emotion categories \(happiness, sadness, anger, fear, surprise, disgust, and neutral\) from audio speech signals with high accuracy across diverse conditions.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (A hybrid CNN-LSTM model is proposed: CNNs capture frequency-domain features from mel-spectrograms, while LSTMs model temporal dependencies. The complete pipeline includes audio preprocessing, feature extraction \(MFCCs, spectral, prosodic features\), and classification. Training utilizes augmentation techniques, cross-validation, and hyperparameter tuning. Evaluation is performed on benchmark datasets \(RAVDESS, CREMA-D, SAVEE, EMO-DB\) using standard metrics, with robustness against noisy conditions also tested.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The expected outcome is state-of-the-art recognition accuracy with real-time computational efficiency for practical deployment. This work demonstrates deep learning effectiveness for emotionally intelligent systems in areas such as mental health monitoring, customer service, adaptive learning, and human-robot interaction, contributing to more empathetic AI.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
