211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 132 0 R
/E (We are motivated by the challenge of non-intrusive mental health monitoring, a clear societal need. Globally, an estimated 5.7% of adults suffer from depression, and nearly 1 in 7 people live with a mental disorder. We have seen how difficult it is to detect the onset of distress early. Our goal is to deploy this technology to passively monitor a patient's voice during routine telehealth or elder care interactions, automatically flagging subtle changes in sadness or anxiety levels for clinicians, thus providing a critical, early-warning system and helping to address the massive burden of mental health conditions.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
