299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (This project implements a robust Speech Emotion Recognition \(SER\) system utilizing a hybrid deep learning architecture designed for cross-speaker generalization. The pipeline begins with advanced, adaptive audio preprocessing on combined RAVDESS and CREMA-D datasets, employing SNR estimation and spectral subtraction to clean low-quality audio, alongside Voice Activity Detection to segment the speech. Features are extracted as 3-channel Log-Mel Spectrograms \(Mel + Delta + Delta-Delta\) and augmented on-the-fly during training with techniques like pitch shift and time stretch. The core of the system is a CNN-BiLSTM-Transformer model, where the CNN extracts local features, the BiLSTM captures short-term temporal context, and the Transformer's attention mechanism models global, long-range dependencies for the final classification into six standardized emotions. The model is trained using PyTorch with an Early Stopping mechanism and rigorously evaluated using speaker-independent data splits to ensure high Accuracy and Weighted F1-Scores on the test set.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 140 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/A [554 0 R 0]
/K [2]
>>
endobj
